        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: जरा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जरा — jarā — \"old age\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जरायां केशाः श्वेताः भवन्ति। jarāyāṃ keśāḥ śvetāḥ bhavanti. In old age the hair turns white."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जरा (jarā) comes from the root √jṝ, \"to grow old\"; MW gives \"the act of becoming old, old age\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
